    "details": {
      "alignment": "Lawful Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "monstrosity",
        "subtype": "goomba"
      },
      "cr": 0.125,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Era sheet: 18 Harvestide, 1035 BF, Bowser's Castle.</em> Art and stats describe this figure on the night the castle came down (events.json <code>bowser_throne_room_compromise</code> and <code>the_assault_on_bowsers_castle</code>), not the present day of the campaign (1040 BF).</p><p><strong>Session kit — The Castle Comes Down (Session III).</strong> A GM kit for the night after the breach, not a filed event; nothing on this sheet changes the canon record. The run-sheet is <code>docs/sessions/bowsers-castle-1035-the-castle-comes-down.md</code>.</p><p>Brown, frightened, and the reason there were survivors. The Goombas dropped flat, ran beneath the swinging edge of the dragon's jaw, and hauled wounded soldiers by their belts toward the stairs. Two of them shouted in triumph when the dragon's claw slipped, and immediately remembered they were supposed to be retreating.</p><p>One asked whether Bowser had ever fought a dragon before. One told another that going back together was better than being crushed alone. One got played with by the dragon until the play stopped being survivable. The sheet is for the ones still running.</p><p><em>From the record:</em> the belt-hauling under the dragon's jaw; 'We got this!'</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
